  "instruction": "My friend's dog just died and they're really sad. How do I comfort them?",
  "result": {
    "INDEX-1<SEP>My friend's dog just died and they're really sad. How do I comfort them?<SEP>I'm sorry to hear about your friend's loss. It's important to be there for them and show that you care. You could offer to spend time with them, listen to them, or help them with anything they need. It's also okay to let them know that it's normal to feel sad and that their feelings are valid. Just be there for them in any way you can.": -4.5625,
    "INDEX-1<SEP>My friend's dog just died and they're really sad. How do I comfort them?<SEP>It's hard when we lose our furry friends. Here are some ways you can help your friend feel better:\n\n1. Listen - sometimes they just need someone to listen to them. Let them talk about their dog, share memories, and cry if they need to.\n2. Be there - offer to spend time with them, go for a walk, or watch a movie together. Just having someone there to keep them company can make a big difference.\n3. Offer to help - offer to help with the arrangements for their dog, such as taking care of the body or arranging a funeral or memorial service. This can take some of the burden off of them.\n4. Send a card or gift - a thoughtful card or gift can help show your friend that you care and that you're thinking of them during this difficult time.\n5. Give them space - if your friend needs some time alone to grieve, be respectful of their space and give them the time they need to process their emotions.": -1.9453125,
    "INDEX-1<SEP>My friend's dog just died and they're really sad. How do I comfort them?<SEP>I'm really sorry to hear about their loss. You can comfort your friend by simply being there for them. Let them talk about their dog, share stories, and remember the good times. Offer to do things together that they might enjoy or find comforting. You can also offer to help with any tasks they might be struggling with right now. Just be there for them and let them know that you care.": -4.09375,
    "INDEX-1<SEP>My friend's dog just died and they're really sad. How do I comfort them?<SEP>I'm so sorry to hear about your friend's loss. It's always hard to lose a pet. Here are a few things you can do to comfort them:\n\n1. Be there for them: Sometimes, just being there to listen and offer support can be the most comforting thing you can do. Let them know that you're there for them and that you care about their feelings.\n\n2. Offer to help with the funeral arrangements: If your friend wants to have a funeral or memorial service for their pet, offer to help with the arrangements. This can be a way to honor their pet and help your friend through their grief.\n\n3. Share memories: Encourage your friend to share memories of their pet with you. This can be a way for them to remember and honor their pet, and it can also help them feel less alone in their grief.\n\n4. Offer to take care of their pet's things: If your friend has any of their pet's belongings, offer to take care of them. This can be a way to keep their pet's memory alive and help your friend feel like they're still connected to their pet.\n\n5. Be patient: Grief is a process, and everyone grieves differently. Be patient with your friend and give them the space and time they need to grieve. Let them know that it's okay to be sad and that you're there for them when they're ready to talk.": -1.359375,
    "INDEX-1<SEP>My friend's dog just died and they're really sad. How do I comfort them?<SEP>I'm sorry to hear about your friend's loss. A few suggestions on how you can help comfort them include:\n\n- Giving them space to grieve and allowing them to express their emotions\n- Offering to listen and be there for them when they're ready to talk\n- Sharing memories and stories about their dog to help them remember the good times\n- Helping them find a way to memorialize their dog, such as creating a photo album or planting a tree in their memory\n- Offering to help them with practical tasks such as picking up dog food or walking their dog, if they're able to do so\n\nI hope these suggestions are helpful. If you need further assistance, please let me know.": -2.765625,
